  "durationSeconds": 61.708333,
  "caption": "Is it bad that I’m having a hard time finding interest in people anymore? #relationship #relatable #fyp #venting",
  "transcript": {
    "text": "It's a bad that I don't really find interest in people anymore. Like I'll meet somebody, we'll talk, they might be attractive, they might be cool, but I just don't feel it anymore. And sometimes I wonder if there's something wrong with me because there was a time when I actually wanted to get to know people, I wanted to learn everything about somebody, like that was exciting to me. But now, I can meet somebody and genuinely enjoy your company, and still not want anything beyond that. And I don't know if that's maturity, or if I just became detached. Maybe I've gotten to a point where attraction isn't enough anymore because I realized that just because you're interested in somebody, doesn't mean they're good for you. And just because somebody gives you attention, doesn't mean that you need to build a connection with them. But then sometimes I ask myself, am I genuinely content being alone, or have I gotten too comfortable not letting anybody close? Because there's a difference. Maybe I'm not losing interest in people. Maybe I'm just becoming more selective about who I give my energy to, and honestly, I think I'm still figuring out which one it is.",
    "segments": null,
    "timing": "unavailable"
